# What changed in each FRIDAY version, newest first, in plain words: a
# "## X.Y.Z" line, then one "- " line per change people will notice. After an
# update FRIDAY shows the lines since the version you last saw, once
# (friday whats-new shows them again).
## 0.10.0
- Setup lets you pick your file manager, terminal, video, picture and PDF apps, code editors and AI coding agents (VS Code, Zed, Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, agy, Cline, Kilo…), and more apps.
- Setup asks your git name and email, and can keep an encrypted daily backup in a private GitHub repo (friday backup github).
- Installing shows a real progress bar: how much is downloaded, how fast, and each app as it goes in.
- Smoother FRIDAY Shell: drawers open quickly and slide from one to the next, notifications fade out, the answer card no longer bounces while it streams.
- Restart and Power off ask you to press again; the password card is clearer.
- Icon buttons say what they do when you hover them; text is easier to read; the clock stays centred over the calendar.
- The lock screen shows a staggered clock, what's playing and the battery.
- Super+I opens FRIDAY Settings, with every key and every command in one place.
- Click one control and ask about it: only that part of the window is sent.
- An answer about a window shows the exact line it relied on.
- Drop a text file or PDF on the ask box to ask about it.
- Tap Super+Shift+Y twice to keep voice typing on; the last 20 dictations stay here to get one back.
- Spoken answers can be brief, normal or detailed.
- "What did you tell me about X last week?" finds past answers with their dates.
- Password and card fields are painted over before a screenshot leaves.
- Two coding agents can try one task, each in its own copy, and you keep the better one.
- friday doctor --fix restarts what's stopped and checks again.
